  "id": "delivery/a-channel-s-breaker-opens-once-five-of-its-deliveries-in-a-row-failed",
  "title": "A channel's deliveries go on through its failures while its breaker is closed; a success between them starts the count again, and the fifth failure in a row opens the breaker, which emits circuit_breaker_opened once, naming the channel and the open state",
  "rules": [
    "§13.1",
    "§8.2"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-13.1-004",
    "RK-13.1-007",
    "RK-13.1-012",
    "RK-8.2-043"
  ],
  "notes": "The breaker's threshold and cooldown are the RFC's defaults (§13.1), the only ones both implementations have. Four failures, a success, then five failures: every one of the ten reaches the channel, and only the fifth failure after the success opens the breaker. What an open breaker does with a delivery is delivery/an-open-breaker-fails-a-delivery-at-once-without-sending-it.",
